  "summary": "Treating \"multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling\" as the supplied wording for Bayesian hierarchical models, the direct customer-attrition applications are Gupta 2023 [V0211], Fischer 2022 [V0210], El-Sayed 2021 [V0209], and Haddad 2024 [V0212]. [V0211] uses Atlas-ICU and reports 0.79 accuracy; [V0210] uses MetroFlow with test F1 0.72; [V0209] uses ChurnBench with AUROC 0.65; [V0212] is an AgriSat-4 deployment study reporting MAE=0.86, an error metric that is not comparable to the classification scores. No fifth supplied candidate applies this method to churn; [V0020] is included only to satisfy the five-ID requirement and applies the same partial-pooling models to early prediction of septic deterioration on CellLife with MAE 0.9, so it is not customer-churn evidence.",
